Doug,

Thanks again for taking the time today, and I'm glad you're back on your fe=
et feeling better. It's always great to connect with someone on your side o=
f the table to get real feedback and insights into what is actually importa=
nt. Before we meet again, I'll prototype the parent/child layer you mention=
ed, so you have something concrete to react to:

  *   DoC sets the mandated fields once and locks them, so every bureau rep=
orts the same things in the same format
  *   Each bureau can add to and tailor the form underneath that, and gover=
n its own use cases
  *   A cross-bureau roll-up that shows DoC leadership where each bureau st=
ands, what stage things are at, and what's been signed off, without anyone =
managing it day to day
I'd love to get a 60-minute working session on the calendar during the week=
 of July 20. Please let me know what your schedule looks like. I did a quic=
k Google and found the public 2025 AI use-case inventory guidance and field=
 set on OMB's GitHub (github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-In=
ventory<https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventor=
y>), which reads as the companion to M-25-21. Please let me know if this is=
 what you were talking about. I'll build the mock-up directly to those fiel=
ds, and the only thing I'd need from you is whatever Commerce layers on top=
 of it and how you format it.

Thanks again and have a great Fourth of July.

Best,



